    <listOfParameters>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="f_renal_function" name="renal function" value="1" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <blockquote>
              <p>1.0: increased kidney function
1.0: normal kidney function (healthy control)
&lt;1.0: decreased kidney function</p>
            </blockquote>
            <p>Renal function relative to the healthy glomerular filtration rate
GFR_base, which is 101 ml/min at 75 kg; a measured creatinine
clearance of X ml/min is the renal function X/101.</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
      </parameter>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="GFR_base" name="glomerular filtration rate (healthy)" value="101" units="ml_per_min" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000002" id="fu_pra" name="fraction unbound in plasma pravastatin" value="0.5" units="dimensionless" constant="true"/>
      <parameter sboTerm="SBO:0000009" id="PRAEX_f" name="renal clearance of unbound pravastatin relative to the GFR" value="16.5960789851112" units="dimensionless" constant="true">
        <notes>
          <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
            <p>The renal clearance of pravastatin is PRAEX_f times the filtration of
its unbound fraction, fu_pra * GFR: 1 is filtration alone, above 1 a
net tubular secretion (OAT3). The clearance from the plasma of the
kidney is limited by the renal plasma flow, so the effective renal
clearance of 0.42-0.46 l/min (Singhvi1990) needs a value of about 16
(fitted).</p>
          </body>
        </notes>
        <distrib:listOfUncertainties>
          <distrib:uncertainty distrib:name="fit PK_20261019_164944__7b050">
            <notes>
              <body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
                <p>The value of <code>KI__PRAEX_f</code> is the result of the fit <code>PK_20261019_164944__7b050</code>, its uncertainty is the profile likelihood of the fit.</p>
                <p>| | |
|---|---|
| fit | <code>PK_20261019_164944__7b050</code> |
| record | <code>PK_20261019_164944__7b050/</code> |
| cost | 53.5273 |
| data points | 196 |
| value | 16.5961 dimensionless |
| bounds | [1, 60] |
| scale | LOG10 |
| method | profile likelihood |
| identifiability | identifiable |
| 95 % confidence interval | [11.6757, 23.5464] |
| Fisher confidence interval | [12.7307, 21.6351] |
| distribution of the draws | <code>lognormal(2.8091664617453405, 0.17894758565872768, 1.0, 60.0)</code> |</p>
              </body>
            </notes>
            <distrib:uncertSpan distrib:name="95 % confidence interval (profile likelihood)" distrib:units="dimensionless" distrib:type="confidenceInterval" distrib:valueLower="11.6757042048921" distrib:valueUpper="23.5463722755267"/>
            <distrib:uncertParameter distrib:name="standard error (Fisher information)" distrib:value="2.23087727950007" distrib:units="dimensionless" distrib:type="standardError"/>
            <distrib:uncertParameter distrib:name="distribution of the draws" distrib:type="distribution">
              <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
                <apply>
                  <csymbol encoding="text" definitionURL="http://www.sbml.org/sbml/symbols/distrib/lognormal"> lognormal </csymbol>
                  <cn> 2.80916646174534 </cn>
